llvm-3.7.1 local rule: a load of a thread-local variable is not a bonus instruction of FoldBranchToCommonDest

This patch CHANGES OPTIMISATION where a branch tests a thread-local flag after
another test with a common successor: `if ((flags & 4) || D_16dc098)`.
3.7.1's SimplifyCFG (FoldBranchToCommonDest, SimplifyCFG.cpp:2057, one bonus
instruction allowed at 2124) hoists the flag's load into the first test's
block and joins the two tests (`or i1`); the base keeps the flag's load
behind the first test. Every other speculation of such a load is unchanged
(LICM, FoldTwoEntryPHINode, SpeculativelyExecuteBB: isSafeToSpeculativelyExecute
is not touched). No upstream state: 3.8.1 to 9.0.0's opt -O2 fold the same
unit (round 296C, c296/ctlu/u618_<v>.ll).

Census of the base (round 296C, c296/addrpos.tsv, win098.tsv, common.py):
code generation splits a branch on `or i1 (test), (load)` back into two
branches and leaves the thread-local's address (the general-dynamic call,
the linker's initial-exec pair in the base) BEFORE the first branch, the
load after it (measured on 0x858390 and 0xcbc5a0); unfolded IR puts the
address after. Of the base's 1,158 reads of D_16dc098, 909 have the address
before the bit-4 branch (IR folded; 903 read `movb; xorb 1; testb 1`, a
negated bool: the inline usable test) and 200 after it (IR two blocks; 187
read `movzbl; and 1; cmp 1`: a plain if). The module's five sites under
this rule: 0x618b00, 0xb1a200, 0xcb8240 unfolded as the base, 0x858390 and
0xcbc5a0 still folded (another route) as the base. A rule in
isSafeToSpeculativelyExecute (every speculation) unfolds 0xcbc5a0 against
the base (its address moves behind the branch) and contradicts the 909.

Swept alone over the two-stage game module (form Lou, round 296C, probe
option -tlg-tls-nobonus at stage 1 and the link, 6,721 functions): 3
functions change: 0x618b00 and 0xb1a200 become equal, draft 0xcb8240 11/162
to 51/159; no row lost.

diff -ru a/lib/Transforms/Utils/SimplifyCFG.cpp b/lib/Transforms/Utils/SimplifyCFG.cpp
--- a/lib/Transforms/Utils/SimplifyCFG.cpp
+++ b/lib/Transforms/Utils/SimplifyCFG.cpp
@@ -2112,6 +2112,13 @@
       continue;
     if (!I->hasOneUse() || !isSafeToSpeculativelyExecute(I))
       return false;
+    // A load of a thread-local variable is not a bonus instruction: it is
+    // left behind its own branch.
+    if (const LoadInst *LI = dyn_cast<LoadInst>(I))
+      if (const GlobalVariable *GV = dyn_cast<GlobalVariable>(GetUnderlyingObject(
+              LI->getPointerOperand(), BB->getModule()->getDataLayout())))
+        if (GV->isThreadLocal())
+          return false;
     // I has only one use and can be executed unconditionally.
     Instruction *User = dyn_cast<Instruction>(I->user_back());
     if (User == nullptr || User->getParent() != BB)
